  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GEO: Design Youth Livelihood: Create and Employ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the development of professional orientation and career development system for the effective employment in the Adjara region. The main objective of the project is to increase the competitiveness of young people through strengthening self-esteem, labour market orientation, job search and self-presentation skills; and to promote operational and effective communication between employers and job seekers, supporting vocational and higher education institutions. Within the framework of the project, young people aged 18-29 living in the Adjara region will undergo a training program consisting of three main modules: career development and employment skills, financial literacy and entrepreneurship. Within the framework of the training program, young people will receive new knowledge, acquire employment skills and develop personal and professional values, which will ensure the improvement of their financial awareness, employment opportunities and economic independence.</narrative>
  </description>
